%[text] Tumor stage: not significantly associated with DFS event status, altough some early-stage groups showed different event proportions. The groups contain very few patients so the results should not be overinterpreted.
%[text] Tumor grade: no statistically significant association with DFS event status.
%[text] Residual disease: clear relationship with recurrence/progression. The even proportion increased from 58.8% in patients with no macroscopic disease to 86.7% in patients with residual disease \>20 mm and the association was statistically significant. 
%%
%[text] 4\. Kaplan-Meier survival analysis for clinical variables
%[text] - Do patients remain disease-free for different lenghts of time? \
%%\ TUMOR STAGE
validStage = clinical_dfs.TUMOR_STAGE_2009 ~= "NA";

time = clinical_dfs.DFS_MONTHS(validStage);
event = dfsEvent(validStage);

stage = categorical( ...
    clinical_dfs.TUMOR_STAGE_2009(validStage));

stage = reordercats(stage, { ...
    'IIA','IIB','IIC','IIIA','IIIB','IIIC','IV'});

stageGroups = categories(stage);

figure; %[output:7937f59e]
hold on; %[output:7937f59e]

for i = 1:numel(stageGroups)

    idx = stage == stageGroups{i};

    censored = ~event(idx);

    [f,x] = ecdf( ...
        time(idx), ...
        "Censoring", censored, ...
        "Function", "survivor");

    stairs(x, f, "LineWidth", 1.5); %[output:7937f59e]

end

xlabel("Disease-free survival (months)"); %[output:7937f59e]
ylabel("Disease-free survival probability"); %[output:7937f59e]
title("Kaplan-Meier curves by tumor stage"); %[output:7937f59e]

legend(stageGroups, "Location", "best"); %[output:7937f59e]
grid on; %[output:7937f59e]
hold off; %[output:7937f59e]

saveas(gcf, "figures/kaplanmeier_tumorstage.png"); %[output:7937f59e]
%[text] Tumor stage: substantial overlap between groups, no clear separation in disease-free survival is visible. Early stage curbes are unstable due to these groups having only a few patients.
