%[text] Residual disease: patients with no macroscopic residual disease show the highest disease-free survival probability over time. The residual-disease groups show poorer DFS and overlap with each other. Formal survival comparison is required to test if the curves differ significantly. 
%%
%[text] 5\. Log-rank test by tumor stage
%[text] note: function at the bottom of the script
validStage = clinical_dfs.TUMOR_STAGE_2009 ~= "NA";

stageTime = clinical_dfs.DFS_MONTHS(validStage);
stageEvent = dfsEvent(validStage);

stage = categorical( ...
    clinical_dfs.TUMOR_STAGE_2009(validStage));

stage = reordercats(stage, { ...
    'IIA','IIB','IIC','IIIA','IIIB','IIIC','IV'});

[chi2_stage, p_stage, df_stage] = ...
    logrankTest(stageTime, stageEvent, stage);

fprintf("\nLog-rank test - Tumor stage\n"); %[output:832173f4]
fprintf("Chi-square = %.3f\n", chi2_stage); %[output:42cf6ba0]
fprintf("Degrees of freedom = %d\n", df_stage); %[output:790c1551]
fprintf("p-value = %.4g\n", p_stage); %[output:2a205df6]
%[text] The log-rank test showed significant difference in DFS across tumor stage groups, suggesting that survival overtime differs by stage. But interpretation should remain cautious as several groups contain very few patients. 
%[text] 
